From 33a9e561246b797a1fc9d3c2dd749aaf0f35c114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:42:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fence a worker's graph/lifecycle calls after its
 own run ended; say "run over" on success [daveey]

agent-6ab88d2b1c (incident t_01a1a57922c2ba77 run 158177): a worker parked with
kanban_block(kind='dependency'), then kanban_unlink'ed that parent (the card was promoted back to
READY), then tried kanban_block(kind='time') and kanban_schedule. Both were refused "unknown id or not
in running/ready/triage" although the card was READY: the real cause, the ended run, was never named.

- tools/kanban_tools_run_end.py (new): ended_run() reads the worker's own task_runs row
  (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK + HERMES_KANBAN_RUN_ID; ended_at set). refusal() returns
  code=run_already_ended with run_id, run_outcome and the card's current status (schedule keeps the
  human-answer way out). with_success_fields() adds run_ended=true + next="This run is over; the card
  is <status>. ..." to a success that ended the caller's own run.
- _worker_guard: block/schedule/continue/move/request_review/request_changes refuse up front with
  run_already_ended once the worker's run ended. kanban_complete is exempt (keeps parked_by_own_run).
- _kanban_handler: every successful run-lifecycle result for the worker's own run carries
  run_ended/next (block, schedule, complete, continue, move, request_review). The read runs only for a
  bound worker and, since the transition is already committed, a failed read returns the original success.
- kanban_link/kanban_unlink: a worker whose run ended may not edit an edge on its OWN card.
  Orchestrators (no HERMES_KANBAN_TASK), live workers, unbound workers and links between two other
  cards are unchanged.
- schemas: kanban_block says it ends the run; kanban_unlink says it is refused once the run ended.

Contract change: test_worker_blocks_on_dependency_then_unlinks_and_completes (block -> unlink ->
complete) encoded the flow that undid the park; it now unlinks while the run is live, and
test_old_run_cannot_complete_once_the_card_was_reclaimed does its unlink as an orchestrator.

Proof:
- RED: new tests/tools/test_kanban_post_run_calls.py 14/14 failed on 221510a25b3; GREEN 27/27 (incl. request_changes fence, failed-annotation keeps success, no reads for non-workers).
- 116 kanban test files: 2769 pass before the expectation updates; the 3 failures were the old contract
  (exact success dict, refusal wording, post-park unlink), updated above.
- 19 mutants (every added condition) killed.
- Independent pinned-Opus review of f0dfa46: approve; its notes (masked committed success on a failed
  annotation read, extra DB opens for non-workers, untested request_changes fence) are fixed here.
- Replay over hub state.db (12,727 kanban sessions, deduped re-persisted rows) + all hub boards'
  task_runs: 0 lifecycle successes after the caller's run ended (the up-front fence only rewords 17
  real refusals, incl. 857674/857697 of the incident); 16 post-end graph successes, 13 on the worker's
  own card (now refused, incl. the incident's 857664) and 3 linking two other cards (unchanged).
